From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: flush offloaded mesh paths on restart

With NSS mesh offload the driver keeps the mesh path table in NSS. A
firmware restart recreates the NSS mesh object with an empty table, but
mac80211 keeps its own paths. It only sends ADD when it creates a path,
so everything after the restart is an UPDATE for an entry NSS no longer
has ("failed to update mpath entry", wifi_mesh_not_found). The
encapsulation path then has no route and the bench stops transmitting
to its mesh peer: after a hw-restart, 0/10 pings three times in a row.

When a mesh interface is reconfigured on a device that offloads mesh
paths, flush its path tables. The paths are rediscovered and re-added.
---
--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -2131,6 +2131,14 @@
 			}
 			fallthrough;
 		case NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT:
+			/* A driver that offloads the mesh path table rebuilds it
+			 * empty on restart, so later UPDATEs of our paths fail and
+			 * the peer becomes unreachable. Flush ours so the paths are
+			 * rediscovered and added to the driver again.
+			 */
+			if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT &&
+			    ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw, SUPPORTS_MESH_NSS_OFFLOAD))
+				mesh_path_flush_by_iface(sdata);
 			if (sdata->vif.bss_conf.enable_beacon) {
 				changed |= BSS_CHANGED_BEACON |
 					   BSS_CHANGED_BEACON_ENABLED;
